    "message": "Revenue is up about 32.0% year to date: $4,556,849 this year against $3,452,838 last year. For the comparable stores alone, growth is about 7.4%: $3,543,155 against $3,299,245.\n\nHow I measured it:\n- **Revenue basis:** pre-tax sales (SUM(subtotal)/100), so sales tax is excluded.\n- **Date range:** the latest order is from 29 Oct 2026, so this year covers 1 Jan to 29 Oct 2026. Last year covers the same days, 1 Jan to 29 Oct 2025.\n- **Comparable stores:** the four stores that were open before 1 Jan 2025 — Philadelphia, Brooklyn, Chicago and San Francisco.\n\nMost of the gap between the two growth figures comes from New Orleans and Los Angeles. New Orleans opened in May 2025, so last year's figures only include part of a year for it. Los Angeles opened in November 2025, so it had no sales at all in last year's period.\n\nTwo judgement calls:\n- **October included:** the data stops on 29 Oct, which is close to the end of the month. Because you asked for both years up to the same day, I counted October rather than dropping it as an unfinished month. If you'd rather stop at 30 September, the figures would change.\n- **Store opening dates:** I used the dates in the stores table, which differ from the dates in the business notes (for example, Philadelphia is listed as opening in October 2022, not September). This doesn't change which stores count as comparable."
